swarm-core NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

Unreleased

  - Breaking: the six scripts are one command, bin/swarm.  launch.sh
    COMMAND is swarm COMMAND; harvest.sh, dashboard.sh, costs.sh,
    progress.sh and control.sh are swarm harvest, swarm dashboard,
    swarm costs, swarm progress and swarm control.  Nothing is left at
    the old paths.  USAGE, UPGRADING FROM 0.24, has the steps.
  - Rename LICENSE to COPYING and drop .md from the agent system prompt.

0.24.0 (2026-11-11)

  - Breaking: each container gets a workspace volume of its own, an
    engagement uses one Docker daemon, and a new engagement starts only
    on a clean runtime directory.
  - Add 'launch.sh retire [--post-process]', which removes stopped
    containers once nothing lives only in them.
  - Add 'launch.sh cleanup [--discard-uncommitted]', which keeps what
    Git had as recovery refs in the checkout, then deletes the
    engagement.
  - Add control.sh, a versioned interface (swarm-core.control/v1) for
    programs that drive engagements.
  - Resolve the target on the host, once per engagement, and mount it
    read-only in every container.
  - Add 'swarm-target-checkout DIR' to the image, which checks the
    target out from its snapshot.
  - Mirror submodules at any depth; containers check them out offline.
  - Take each submodule mirror from that submodule's Git directory.
  - Join only a complete engagement.
  - Pass docker_args to 'docker run' exactly, check their form first,
    and refuse the engine's own labels.
  - Read 'interactive --agent-index' as a decimal number.
  - Add PI_REASONING=1, which makes effort reach custom Pi models.
  - Add PI_COMPACTION_RESERVE_TOKENS for Pi's compaction reserve.
  - Keep what agents write from steering the host's Git or filling its
    disk.
  - Keep repositories nested in a workspace, and Git checkouts outside
    the volume, through retire and cleanup.
  - Refuse a partial clone in a workspace on cleanup.
  - Stop a workspace scan instead of hanging on what an agent left.
  - Keep in the bare repo and the mirrors what the checkout's branches,
    tags and HEAD reach; start a new bare repo from the checkout's HEAD.
  - Read agent-work from the bare repo in place in progress.sh.
  - Show workspace volumes with no container, and an unfinished
    cleanup, in the dashboard.
  - Run no hook or fsmonitor command of the checkout in harvest.
  - Merge agent work built on the engagement's base after HEAD moved.
  - Keep commits that no push shipped, and move the harness branch
    after a scratch push whenever that loses nothing.
  - Keep the bare repo and the mirrors while interactive sessions are
    open.
  - Let no token reach another engagement through retire, cleanup or
    start.
  - Leave no Git process running that holds the engagement lock.
  - Leave no temporary files behind in launch.sh.
  - Say there is nothing to stop when 'launch.sh stop' finds no runtime
    directory.
  - Do not take a repository nested in an uninitialized submodule's
    directory for uncommitted work in cleanup.
  - Exit nonzero when Bash 3.2 stops a script on an unset variable.
  - Print no "stopped before its end" message when a signal ends a
    script on Bash 4.1 and later.
  - Keep the caller's Pi settings out of the tests; fix
    tests/runtime_pi.sh on Linux hosts whose UID is not 1000.

0.23.0 (2026-11-03)

  - Rename claude-swarm to swarm-core.
  - Breaking: move engine state out of /tmp.
  - Breaking: write the state file as JSON.
  - Breaking: allow one checkout per project id; add SWARM_PROJECT.
  - Breaking: add the engagement lock.
  - Add engagement ids.
  - Add the pi driver.
  - Support Codex subscriptions through Pi.
  - Add a configurable Pi request timeout and in-session retry.
  - Retry Pi OAuth validation during credential refresh.
  - Restart an exited post-process with dashboard 'p'.
  - Fix costs.sh with an effort level on macOS.
  - Start no post-process driver without post_process.
  - Do not split a submodule mirror mount on a space.
  - Create transient files with mktemp.
  - Keep project ids ASCII in every locale.
  - Copy the checkout's objects into the bare repo and the mirrors.
  - Harvest again after merging an interactive branch.
  - Fix tests when host and agent UIDs differ, and checks that failed
    now and then under load.

0.22.0 (2026-06-08)

  - Breaking: swap the dashboard's post-process keys; 'P' tails the
    logs and 'p' starts the run.
  - Base the agent image on Debian trixie and install unzip in it.
  - Tag a restore point in harvest before merging.
  - Add post_process.setup to override the post-process setup.
  - Document the dashboard effort letters.

0.21.1 (2026-06-08)

  - Propagate the container's exit code from post-process.

0.21.0 (2026-05-26)

  - Add interactive agent containers for human-guided work:
    'launch.sh interactive', chat and shell.
  - Handle Docker errors in the dashboard's missing-container check.
  - Include every swarm container in the stop controls.
  - Skip interactive-only profiles in dashboard state summaries.
  - Avoid setup-log conflicts in the manual interactive harvest test.
  - Remove the scheduled full CI matrix.

0.20.16 (2026-05-26)

  - Sanitize Docker project names for uppercase repo basenames.
  - Show configured post-processing before it starts.
  - Give dashboard post-process logs a shortcut of their own.
  - Document that 'launch.sh wait' does not start agents.

0.20.15 (2026-05-16)

  - Keep agent commits on a fatal-error exit and on 'docker stop'.
  - Verify the runtime emergency push under --all.

0.20.14 (2026-05-06)

  - Rebuild the post-process image when the driver set changes.
  - Do not re-introduce in harvest.sh commits that an upstream
    force-push dropped.

0.20.13 (2026-04-28)

  - Treat Codex "Selected model is at capacity" as retriable.

0.20.12 (2026-04-28)

  - Sign Codex agents' commits when signing_key is configured.
  - Add Codex CLI version pinning.
  - Isolate scratch-repo unit tests from the host's gitconfig.

0.20.11 (2026-04-24)

  - Do not send the operator to harvest.sh from the bare-repo preflight
    when local HEAD is strictly ahead of the bare repo.

0.20.10 (2026-04-23)

  - Suppress hooks in the session-end rebase and push, which failed
    every retry when the target installs worktree-touching hooks.

0.20.9 (2026-04-23)

  - Force the C numeric locale in dashboard.sh, costs.sh and the
    harness, which died where ',' is the decimal separator.

0.20.8 (2026-04-23)

  - Do not abort the harvest.sh preview on a large commit log.

0.20.7 (2026-04-22)

  - Retry Codex SSE stream drops when max_retry_wait is set.
  - Park cherry-pick conflicts in the scratch push instead of dropping
    the agent's commits.

0.20.6 (2026-04-21)

  - Suppress hooks in the scratch push's 'worktree add'.

0.20.5 (2026-04-20)

  - Fall back to cherry-picking onto a scratch worktree when the
    session-end rebase exhausts its retries.
  - Add an activity watchdog for silent CLI hangs.
  - Grow test coverage.

